<?php

namespace Illuminate\Http;

/**
 * Docuccino stub: give JsonResponse a payload type parameter (and a folded HTTP
 * status parameter) so the shape and status recovered by
 * ResponseJsonReturnTypeExtension have somewhere to live. Pairs with that
 * extension (design §7). Shipped in the generated neon's `stubFiles`.
 *
 * `TStatus` carries the constant-folded response status when it is statically
 * known (`response()->json($x, 201)` → `JsonResponse<TPayload, 201>`); it
 * defaults to `200` at the call site. The pipeline unwraps these parameters,
 * mapping the payload shape under the folded status.
 *
 * A THIRD parameter `TContentType` is populated only by ResponseShapeRefiner
 * (helper-indirection recovery) when a helper set an explicit `Content-Type`
 * header (e.g. `new JsonResponse($body, $status, ['Content-Type' =>
 * 'application/problem+json'])`) — it is not produced by the
 * `response()->json()` extension, which emits the first two only. The pipeline
 * hoists the payload schema under the recovered media type (default
 * `application/json`).
 *
 * The refiner's own `ClassT` carries a FOURTH argument (the constructor
 * arguments an object payload was built with) that deliberately has no
 * `@template` here: it is written by the refiner and read by the pipeline, never
 * round-tripped through PHPStan, so no generic has to hold it.
 *
 * @template TPayload
 * @template TStatus of int
 * @template TContentType of string
 */
class JsonResponse extends \Symfony\Component\HttpFoundation\JsonResponse
{
}
